Remember that `Debug.Assert` works at runtime if the DEBUG preprocessor directive is defined. If it is not defined, the assertions will effectively become no-ops, i.e., they will not cause the program to crash and the execution will continue as usual. This is useful for testing purposes to catch potential bugs that will cause a program to crash in a Release build.--------------------Based on the provided C# code, here is the corresponding output for the assert statement:

